 "summary": "The exposed surface is minimal and fully characterized: bodies are unexposed, every projection and definitional restatement uses `:= (rfl)`, the cos/sin, orientation-reversal and boost lemmas let consumers use `azimuth` and `trento` without unfolding, and `@[ext]` is sound because `AzimuthalFrame` carries no data its operations ignore. One non-blocking note: `SIDIS` now holds two representations of (\u03c6_h, \u03c6_S) \u2014 `Real.Angle` here and `\u211d` in the pre-existing `Asymmetries/Harmonics.lean` \u2014 which Layer 5 will have to reconcile, but a bridge cannot live in this Layer-0 module without inverting the dependency.",
